  "title": "# Build: notes-tasks-calendar ## Brett said (verbatim) \"In the notes, task manager and to-do (one p…",
  "asked": "# Build: notes-tasks-calendar ## Brett said (verbatim) \"In the notes, task manager and to-do (one plugin), we're gonna add a calendar where we can set events and schedules. We can set weekly schedules. And it's gonna be hooked up to our Gmail / Google Calendar through axHub's MCP server.\" Base: branch claude/notes-tasks-sync (PR #363, shared notes-tasks plugin); merge it first, build on it. 1. Calendar inside the notes-tasks plugin (console + AmberX): day / week / month / agenda views; events (time, location, notes, reminders); recurring + weekly schedules; tasks with due dates show on it. 2. Two-way sync with Google Calendar through axHub's Google service (build axhub-google, queued). Until that lands, local calendar works on its own; sync switches on when the service exists. 3. Reminders go through the console notifications engine (AmberX only delivers). 4. REST/MCP/CLI + voice commands (UI registry). 5. Tests, README, screenshots to UI Review, PR to the merge queue. Do NOT land directly. One session, lean chain. ## Addendum 1 (Brett, voice) \"I need a really sweet interface for the scheduling stuff, the schedules. Make it sick.\" - Polished, modern calendar UI (framework tokens + theme only): smooth view transitions, drag to create / move / resize events, colour-coded calendars, now-line, mini-month, quick-add bar (plain English: 'gym every Mon Wed 6pm'), weekly schedule editor with drag blocks, phone gestures (swipe days/weeks, long-press drag), dark/light. Phone-first, desktop great too. - Screenshots of every view (phone + desktop) to UI Review. ## Addendum 2 (Brett, voice) \"Open that in its own window with multiple layouts. Open numerous schedules, days and weeks: a week here and a month there, and drag events from here to there. Attach an RSVP list / invite list to an event with a check mark of who's replied. Send automatic emails to RSVP people, or emails asking people to confirm they've read/seen it. It needs to update in the scheduler on AmberX.\" - Calendar opens in its own window (windows@1 / dock@1); multiple panes side by side, each any view/date/calendar; save named layouts; drag events between panes. - Invite / RSVP list per event: guests, status (invited / yes / no / maybe / seen), check marks, counts. Emails sent through axHub Google (Gmail) when it exists: invites, automatic RSVP reminders, read/seen confirmation requests (tracked link). Replies update the event status live on console and AmberX. Sending email = confirm approval (axHub policy). ## Addendum 3 (Brett, voice) \"Any replies to the emails get logged. They type their reply in a text field that's sent in the email; they have to reply in the text field so it gets logged in the system.\" - Each invite/reminder email has a link to a small public reply page (per-guest signed token, no login): RSVP buttons + a text field. Submissions are logged on the event (who, when, answer, message) and update status live on console + AmberX. - Plain email replies are also caught via Gmail (axHub) and logged on the event when possible, but the reply page is the main path. - Reply page is rate-limited, token expires, no other data exposed. Watch live: Brett can watch the screen you are changing hot-render in the console. Whenever you start work on a screen or element, run `node framework/cli/axf.mjs focus <app> [route] [css-selector] --note \"<what you are changing>\"` (apps: console-web, axhub-web, amberx-droid, walkthrough-studio, demo, framework, console, axhub-android, voicevault). Agent cap: heavy steps (pnpm/npm/vite builds, docker node:22 test runs, Playwright) share a VPS-wide lock. Run each one as `node /opt/axf/deploy/../framework/cli/agent-slots.mjs heavy -- <command>` so only a few run at once. Model switches: a downgrade (e.g. Fable → Opus) is fine. Fable upgrades need no approval right now (Brett, Nov 4 2026: \"If it needs Fable, set it to be Fable\"): a step that needs Fable (schemas, asset types, contracts, engines/kernel, cross-app protocols) is set to Fable…",
